.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH ckman-openpgp-keys 1  ckman 
.SH NAME
ckman\-openpgp\-keys \- Manage private keys
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBckman\-openpgp\-keys\fR [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIsubcommands\fR>
.SH DESCRIPTION
Manage private keys
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
ckman\-openpgp\-keys\-info(1)
Show metadata about a private key
.TP
ckman\-openpgp\-keys\-generate(1)
Generate a key pair on the device (replacing any key in the slot)
.TP
ckman\-openpgp\-keys\-import(1)
Import a private key (PEM/DER: PKCS#8, PKCS#1, SEC1)
.TP
ckman\-openpgp\-keys\-set\-touch(1)
Set the touch policy for a key slot
.TP
ckman\-openpgp\-keys\-help(1)
Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)
